        "id": "ch13_6_2-1",
        "text": "Using K3b\nTo create an audio CD using the K3b package, follow these steps:\n1. Start K3b by choosing Applications \u00c1 Multimedia \u00c1 K3b.\nWhen the application starts, you see the window shown in Figure 13-14.\nFIGURE 13-13:\nAdding audio files\nto burn onto the\nCD in Brasero.\nFIGURE 13-14:\nThe K3b CD and\nDVD burner.\n270   PART 3 Getting Things Done\n2. Click the New Audio CD Project option on the main K3b page.\nThe Audio CD window (see Figure 13-15) appears.\n3. In the top section, click the folder button and navigate to the files you\nwant to burn onto the CD.\n4. Drag and drop the files you want to burn into the lower section of the\npage.\nAs you drag files into the lower section, the status bar at the bottom grows,\nshowing you how much space is left on the CD.\n5. When you\u2019re finished, click the Burn button in the lower section.\nThe Audio Project dialog box opens, as shown in Figure 13-16.\n6. Insert a blank CD, select the number of copies you want (if necessary),\nand click the Burn button.\nThe burn process starts copying your digital audio files onto the CD as analog\naudio files.\n7. Remove your new CD from the drive and then click Close to close the\nburn information dialog box, and Close again to close the main burn\ndialog box.\nAfter you\u2019ve completed the burning process, it\u2019s usually a good idea to label the\nCD \u2014 I can\u2019t tell you how many unlabeled CDs I have laying around! Now you can\ntake your audio CD to virtually any CD player to listen to your downloaded files!\nFIGURE 13-15:\nThe K3b Audio CD\nProject window.\nCHAPTER 13 Messing with Audio 271\nFIGURE 13-16:\nThe K3b Audio\nProject\ndialog box.",
